course: dictionary
lesson: 9227
title: Softening words: somewhat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Somewhat means a little, or to some degree. It makes something less strong than it would be otherwise. «I felt somewhat tired after the match» means you were a bit tired, not exhausted.
explain: Compare the words around it. «She was very tired» is strong, but «she was somewhat tired» is softer. Try the swap test: put a little or rather in place of somewhat. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found its meaning.
explain: Writers use somewhat when they want to be careful and polite, especially in reports and exams. «The results were somewhat surprising» means they were a bit surprising, not shocking. Look for phrases like somewhat better, somewhat different and somewhat surprised.
fact: Somewhat means a little, to some degree, or rather.
fact: «Somewhat» is a softening word: «somewhat tired» is less than «very tired».
fact: In formal writing, «somewhat» means fairly, and it makes a statement gentler.
fact: In science, «the temperature rose somewhat» describes a small change, not an exact amount.
fact: The old English suffix «-ish» also means somewhat, as in «childish» and «reddish». Today people also say «7-ish», meaning about 7.
exercise: «The path was somewhat muddy after the rain.» What does somewhat mean here? | Not muddy at all | *A little, to some degree | Completely covered in mud | Very dry and dusty
exercise: In a report, Sam writes «the results were somewhat surprising». Which word could replace somewhat here? | Extremely | Certainly not | *Rather | Suddenly
exercise: Which is the softer way to say «the cake was very good»? | *The cake was somewhat good | The cake was perfect | The cake was extremely good | The cake was the best ever
test: «The temperature rose somewhat during the afternoon.» What does this tell you about the rise? | *It was a small rise, not an exact amount | It fell sharply | It rose by exactly ten degrees | It did not change at all
test: Which phrase from the lesson means slightly different? | Never the same | *Somewhat different | Very, very different | Completely new
exam: The Water Rat says his life feels «somewhat narrow and circumscribed». Circumscribed means closed in and limited, so what does somewhat mean here? | *A little, to some degree | Completely narrow | Very wide and free | Not narrow at all
